WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.760
To explain the difference between child protection and

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.330
child safeguarding, um, it's actually very complicated

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.270
often because in so many languages, we don't have a

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.850
word for safeguarding, but what we kind of do on a

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:14.020
European level what the Council of Europe does, the

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.760
European union and the UN, UNICEF, we've all kind

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.000
of established  safeguarding as kind of an internal

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.060
structure, whilst protection is more external.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:25.890
So when we're talking about protection, we talk

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.534
about the systems, the, their structures around

00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:31.904
kind of anything that has to do with, with the

00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:34.695
country or with the institutions in the country

00:00:34.695 --> 00:00:37.095
and so on, how we protect the children from harm.

00:00:37.364 --> 00:00:39.675
But when we talk about safeguarding, we look inside

00:00:39.675 --> 00:00:41.745
ourselves and we look inside our organization and we

00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:44.385
say, how are we making sure that in anything that we do

00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:47.295
within our organization, we're keeping children safe.

00:00:47.385 --> 00:00:50.205
So when we talk about why safeguarding is

00:00:50.205 --> 00:00:53.685
so important, it is mainly because so many

00:00:53.685 --> 00:00:56.855
people do wrong by not knowing better.

00:00:57.035 --> 00:01:00.705
So a lot of safeguarding breaches that happen simply

00:01:00.705 --> 00:01:02.955
happened because people haven't been taught and they

00:01:02.955 --> 00:01:05.175
haven't been taught to think in a certain direction

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:07.995
and think about the consequences of their actions.

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:11.745
So small things that you might consider to be minimal

00:01:11.745 --> 00:01:14.665
might actually be bigger in, in, in the big context.

00:01:14.985 --> 00:01:17.255
And these are very often things that might seem very

00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:20.134
straightforward, but aren't, and just getting that

00:01:20.134 --> 00:01:22.895
kind of notion into people's head about how we save our

00:01:22.905 --> 00:01:25.414
children and how we make sure that in our interaction,

00:01:25.744 --> 00:01:27.845
um, we are always putting the benefit of the child

00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:28.294
first.

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.824
This also escalates within the individuals.

00:01:30.845 --> 00:01:34.175
So as soon as you start this process and start this thought,

00:01:34.475 --> 00:01:37.175
people then can kind of follow it themselves as well.

